                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "23e3e5d8-2791-3f85-85ee-ca1a00233b18",
                        "entry_id": "2576704a-67a2-330e-ab2d-1ba70d7fdfea",
                        "glosses": [
                            "haniebne, niegodziwe postępowanie; występek zasługujący na potępienie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2da4f547-fdf5-48b4-bbbc-56d8da8ec8b8",
                                "sense_id": "23e3e5d8-2791-3f85-85ee-ca1a00233b18",
                                "text": "Od dawna domyślałem się zdrady, ale pobyt jego w Villaca przekonał mnie o twojej niegodziwości…"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f3e87946-57ec-4254-b582-6144106477a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "2576704a-67a2-330e-ab2d-1ba70d7fdfea",
                        "source_sense_id": "23e3e5d8-2791-3f85-85ee-ca1a00233b18",
                        "target_lang_word": "wickedness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wickedness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a4a6669-c8be-3cd3-93bc-9ba192c52862",
                                        "entry_id": "66bc7051-0eeb-331b-ba5b-f3dab364664c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being wicked; evil disposition; immorality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa9c1ac6-ffd8-4c99-af75-3c0d493da64f",
                                                "sense_id": "3a4a6669-c8be-3cd3-93bc-9ba192c52862",
                                                "text": "So, if a Sonne that is by his Father ſent about Merchandize, doe ſinfully miſcarry vpon the Sea; the imputation of his vvickedneſſe, by your rule, ſhould be impoſed vpon his Father that ſent him: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15ced96c-b2de-4d03-82b6-f2460e267482",
                                                "sense_id": "3a4a6669-c8be-3cd3-93bc-9ba192c52862",
                                                "text": "We speak of wickedness as something in the soul different from virtue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d4fcd5a-6fe4-4bca-8543-48fb83c2604a",
                                                "sense_id": "3a4a6669-c8be-3cd3-93bc-9ba192c52862",
                                                "text": "Derived from the Latin words \"scelero\" — which means crime or wickedness — and \"phobos\" meaning fear — scelerophobia is coined by both criminologists and psychologists as the fear of burglars, according to Ayla Faisal, a clinical psychologist and a PhD scholar at the Institute of Clinical Psychology at the University of Karachi."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e161ca7-5f2d-3b43-aae6-2b4deb3ce5c6",
                                        "entry_id": "66bc7051-0eeb-331b-ba5b-f3dab364664c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wicked or sinful thing or act; morally bad or objectionable behaviour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e71f947b-34ef-4165-ab98-242752342043",
                        "source_entry_id": "2576704a-67a2-330e-ab2d-1ba70d7fdfea",
                        "source_sense_id": "23e3e5d8-2791-3f85-85ee-ca1a00233b18",
                        "target_lang_word": "villainy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "villainy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4c86689-e905-3da1-9db3-55346c3e9c40",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Evil or wicked character or behaviour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30256d4e-3edb-416e-833b-96201df4672b",
                                                "sense_id": "e4c86689-e905-3da1-9db3-55346c3e9c40",
                                                "text": "Mos Eisley spaceport- you will never find a more wretched hive of scum and villainy. We must be cautious."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "99bd7366-8824-3268-9fb5-2fd85fafdc31",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wicked or treacherous act."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f069af8-a0d7-4425-9682-e865e6910423",
                                                "sense_id": "99bd7366-8824-3268-9fb5-2fd85fafdc31",
                                                "text": "He drew from his pocket a pistol, which, devoid of principle or honour, with an assassin-like assault, he instantly aimed at the breast of Lord Deloraine, but which, in the struggle that ensued, as if by retributive justice, went off unexpectedly and lodged its contents in the body of Melliphant,—thus doomed to receive his punishment by his own hand, and by the very weapon he had carried for his own defence in the perpetration of his villanies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46f38302-76d5-354a-917f-04f7e9757c95",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ill-treatment, indignity, degrading or shameful treatment of someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "505dedd1-5b8f-37b8-b7b7-a77ab3980ef0",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Disgrace, ignominy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39c6f7fd-0d62-389b-a923-bb4d18bda7df",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being a villein or serf, and by extension servitude or low estate in life."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54dbf626-43d2-3f00-b28d-25a0608de1e8",
                                        "entry_id": "b76040b7-cedf-3589-92a4-dd94fac60a74",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boorishness, rudeness, bad cultivation or manners."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "villainy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d812aa46-6b5b-3c71-93f0-3f1b283bb317",
                                        "entry_id": "1e37dcf5-3edb-3151-9907-a98c428edc38",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characteristic of a villain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48ddd1a1-bdfd-49f0-84e9-2ec32eaf7d89",
                                                "sense_id": "d812aa46-6b5b-3c71-93f0-3f1b283bb317",
                                                "text": "We are all villainy— very villainy, as I am a Christian man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a86f0c4-0a0b-4975-9e80-55b163898929",
                                                "sense_id": "d812aa46-6b5b-3c71-93f0-3f1b283bb317",
                                                "text": "Apparently, in both domestic and foreign movies, you can't get too villainy to displease an audience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1788a269-5d94-4ff2-842a-63520e6a20f0",
                                                "sense_id": "d812aa46-6b5b-3c71-93f0-3f1b283bb317",
                                                "text": "Yet here, actual reality offers you the worst villain ever and you say, sorry, he is too villainy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b9a6f3e-273d-4ab4-aa2b-59ed04d4ac48",
                        "source_entry_id": "2576704a-67a2-330e-ab2d-1ba70d7fdfea",
                        "source_sense_id": "23e3e5d8-2791-3f85-85ee-ca1a00233b18",
                        "target_lang_word": "knavery",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "knavery",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e2a5a47-28b8-3006-898a-995dc4f70fe3",
                                        "entry_id": "df441f4c-a3e6-332b-a0d8-24de80a4ef08",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The antics or tricks of a knave; boyish mischief."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4769768d-4b6b-4eb5-9cff-6c68b1b6ce0b",
                                                "sense_id": "5e2a5a47-28b8-3006-898a-995dc4f70fe3",
                                                "text": "[…] Harry Monmouth, being in his right wittes and his good iudgements, turn'd away the fat Knight with the great belly doublet: he was full of ieſts, and gypes, and knaueries, and mockes; I haue forgot his name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5021172-9584-4d18-a84c-d160fbfd11d9",
                                                "sense_id": "5e2a5a47-28b8-3006-898a-995dc4f70fe3",
                                                "text": "The young Oxonian, on the contrary, had led out one of his maiden aunts, on whom the rogue played a thousand little knaveries with impunity; he was full of practical jokes, and his delight was to tease his aunts and cousins; yet, like all mad-cap youngsters, he was a universal favourite among the women."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                        "entry_id": "df441f4c-a3e6-332b-a0d8-24de80a4ef08",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An unprincipled action; deceit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13f397ea-827a-4c89-a04e-513317297344",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "Caſsio’s a proper man, let me ſee now, / To get his place and to make vp my will, / A double knauery—how, how,—let me see, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa5d25f5-04e9-4d76-914f-445b80534782",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "[A]s our little Traffick with the Natives was hitherto upon the Faith of their firſt Kindneſs, we found ſome Knavery among them at laſt; for having bought ſome Cattel of them for our Toys, […] one of our Men differing with his Chapman, truly they huff’d him in their Manner, and keeping the things he had offered them for the Cattel, made their Fellows drive away the Cattel before his Face, and laugh at him; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2563655a-19b6-43af-8a71-ef9ee07d3e58",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "He conſider'd juſtly, that it was not requiſite, in order to reject a Fact of this Nature, to be able accurately to diſprove the Teſtimony, and to trace its Falſhood, thro' all the Circumſtances of Knavery and Credulity, which produc'd it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f41462-0be4-4330-97d2-01fe0409b7b2",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "O, Hang 'em—no—wine does but draw forth a man's natural qualities; and to make them drink would only be to whet their Knavery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b8e5660-cf6d-4cb3-999f-bdf6b3c177ca",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "How much is conveyed in those two short words—\"The Parish!\" And with how many tales of distress and misery, of broken fortune, and ruined hopes, too often of unrelieved wretchedness and successful knavery, are they associated!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdeab3e2-c83a-4205-bb60-119280d8efc3",
                                                "sense_id": "84340981-e59d-3545-9e99-c865649ec202",
                                                "text": "I esteem the modern error, That all goes by self-interest and the checking and balancing of greedy knaveries, and that, in short, there is nothing divine whatever in the association of men, a still more despicable error, natural as it is to an unbelieving century, than that of a ‘divine right’ in people called Kings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "657177e2-2c06-4fe8-979f-9406c2bd3e70",
                        "source_entry_id": "2576704a-67a2-330e-ab2d-1ba70d7fdfea",
